{"text": "# Step-by-Step Solution\n\n## Step 1: Calculate 82^9\n\nI need to find 82 raised to the 9th power. I can use efficient exponentiation:\n- 82^2 = 6,724\n- 82^4 = (82^2)^2 = 6,724^2 = 45,212,176\n- 82^8 = (82^4)^2 = 45,212,176^2 = 2,044,142,256,015,376\n- 82^9 = 82^8 \u00d7 82 = 2,044,142,256,015,376 \u00d7 82\n\n## Step 2: Multiply to get 82^9\n\n2,044,142,256,015,376 \u00d7 82 = 167,619,664,993,260,832\n\n## Step 3: Extract and sum the digits\n\nThe number 82^9 = 167,619,664,993,260,832\n\nDigits: 1, 6, 7, 6, 1, 9, 6, 6, 4, 9, 9, 3, 2, 6, 0, 8, 3, 2\n\nSum: 1+6+7+6+1+9+6+6+4+9+9+3+2+6+0+8+3+2 = **92**\n\n```python\nresult = 82 ** 9\ndigit_sum = sum(int(d) for d in str(result))\nprint(digit_sum)\n```\n\n92", "usage": {"calls": 1, "input_tokens": 922, "output_tokens": 2362, "cost_usd": 0.012731999999999999, "latency_s": 20.45032000541687}, "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "stop_reason": "end_turn"}